Hi Andrei - thanks for your patience\! There’s a lot of information to go through, so it took a bit of time. 



# Do we have any legal restrictions in any country to ask users to tip couriers before an order has been delivered? {color:#36b37e}No - as long as the feature is totally voluntary. {color}

2. Can we allow the user to set up a default tip amount for order once and charge them without asking for confirmation in each new order? {color:#36b37e}We can set up a default tip amount, but clients should confirm it per each order. E.g by clicking “include tip” or something like that. Tips should not be automatically included, and should require an active step to confirm by the client per each order. {color}

PS It will be possible to cancel this at the checkout anytime  - {color:#36b37e}it should be the other way around, i.e. it can be enabled at checkout. The EU consumer rights directive 2011/83/EU, Article 22 sets out that “Before the consumer is bound by the contract or offer, the trader shall seek the{color}{color:#36b37e} *express consent of the consumer to any extra payment*{color}{color:#36b37e} in addition to the remuneration agreed upon for the trader’s main contractual obligation.” {color}



3. Do we have any legal restrictions to ask users to tip couriers (or edit/cancel the tip amount which has been charged earlier) for the historical order which has been delivered a few days ago?

{color:#36b37e}How would this look in practice? I.e. would there be a push notification to leave a tip? Why would we ask them to edit or cancel the tip amount? {color}

{color:#36b37e}Overall, it is ok from the legal side to tip for an historical order, in case it is limited to a reasonable timeline. {color}

{color:#36b37e}Regarding editing/cancelling the tip - to avoid any disputes, the tip should be able to be edited/cancelled only before the courier is notified of the tip amount. {color}



4. Do we need to update any of our Agreements (Individual Courier, Courier fleet, Restaurant) to implement the Courier tips feature? 

Do we need to update any of our T&C (Eater, Individual Courier, Courier fleet, Restaurant) to implement the Courier tips feature?

I assume yes - I need to understand the list for every country and the update process.

{color:#36b37e} T&Cs for eaters, restaurants and couriers should be updated. To update the TCs, we need to send a notification to the eaters, restaruants and couriers that we have updated the TCs and the new TCs will come into effect in 30 days.  However, since we don’t want to update TCs too often, we should try to time this update in a way that we can include some other updates in the TCs as well. What is the current ETA for implementation? {color}

{color:#36b37e}For fleets - do I understand correctly that the tips  will be received by the fleet  (similarly to the delivery fee right now) and the fleet will then distribute the tips between the couriers as they see fit? {color}



5. We want to let users refund tips through CS or automatically by pressing the button edit/cancel from the order history interface. Do we have any legal restrictions to do so?

{color:#36b37e}To avoid any disputes, the tip should be able to be edited/cancelled only before the courier is notified of the tip amount or the tip amount is already transferred to the courier. {color}

6. We do have this copy “Couriers get 100% of the tips“ (it is quite a standard phrase for our competitors) but in fact, tips might be subject to Couriers fleets commissions + some Couriers might need to pay taxes from the tip amount received. (all the bank fees on us) Do you recommend using it?

{color:#36b37e}We can still use it - from our side, we still give 100% of the tip to the courier (i.e. we don’t apply commission). The fact that the courier might need to pay income taxes does not change it.{color}

{color:#36b37e}Couriers who work for fleets are a bit more trickier. Do I understand correctly that the tips  will be received by the fleet  (similarly to the delivery fee right now) and the fleet will then distribute the tips between the couriers as they see fit? In such case, the phrase should be something along the lines of “Bolt will not take any commission from the tip amount”.{color} 

7. "The amounts will depend on the city and will be configured through the Admin by local Ops teams. (same as tips for Drivers)" Do you see any legal risks here?

{color:#36b37e}Could you explain that a bit further? What do you mean the amounts will depend on the city - do you mean the recommended amounts or the max amounts?{color}

8. Any risks with tips refund?

{color:#36b37e}Could you explain a bit further? How is this different from the client cancelling the tip? Would Bolt want to cover the cost itself or take the amount from the courier?{color}

9. What details on the part of Legal should we take into account while feature implementation?

{color:#36b37e}All covered above. {color}

