# The escalation rules currently mention a list of things that should be included in the escalation. After that, there is a bullet point mentioning they should be included as internal notes if the escalation is via Zendesk.
At the moment we have two escalation routes for agents, Slack and Zendesk. The two require slightly different things to be included, and the current list is only relevant for Slack - my idea was to create two simple bullet points mentioning Slack requirements: 1,2,3 and Zendesk requirements accordingly. For Slack that would be the ones already present:

* {color:#97a0af}_A brief description of the issue_{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_The investigation completed so far, including a link to the KB article that does not have the answer needed to solve the issue_{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_All relevant ticket, user profile, and order links_{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_The question that needs to be answered_{color}.

For Zendesk they are similar, but not exactly the same: 

* {color:#97a0af}_A brief description of the issue_{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_The investigation completed so far, including a link to the KB article that does not have the answer needed to solve the issue_{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_If the communication was via phone, time-stamps of any relevant events that caused the escalation._{color}
* {color:#97a0af}_The reason for the escalation._{color}

2. In regard to time-stamps, whenever IH get a valid escalation via Zendesk, they have to take it over and assist the user. To do so, they must know what the case is about and most importantly what caused the escalation, as that is usually the bulk of the users' concern. If we receive a 20-40 minute call, the agents do not have time to skim through it looking for the reason it was escalated to verify it, it is much more effective for them to know when the threat or other cause for escalation was mentioned. Knowing this is absolutely essential for the sake of offering assistance to the user, but also for the sake of evaluating the escalation as either valid or invalid. For OS it would take a few seconds to add the timestamp, while for IH it can take an inefficiently long time searching for it on their own.

3. Regarding changing the structure: the feedback regarding escalations is provided on a weekly basis, including outlier agent names, and included in agent retrainings; recently a deep-dive has been shared with Majorel as well to aid in this. Here the question is with convenience: while the article needs to be followed in full, if an agent has read it through once, it is likely that the following times they will try and skim through for the most important parts, regarding things they absolutely have to include in their escalation. In cases when there are high volumes of tickets, or the agent is on a call with a client, it is difficult to find and apply the necessary parts of the article out of a large column of text. However, I fully understand your concern regarding the content, and will defer to your judgement about the structure.

Thanks\!

