Hi [~accountid:61027984a539cb006846c64f], please find the overview of basic requirements below. We are still waiting for the response with respect to data collection requirement. I’ll keep you posted. 

The law firm also went into great detail with requirements for importing nicotine pouches. These do not apply to our business, but I will copy them here for the overview.

----

*Mandatory requirements*. Currently mandatory requirements are only those under [general product safety law|https://likumi.lv/ta/en/en/id/87664-law-on-the-safety-of-goods-and-services]. As well as those under [CLP Regulation|https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:32008R1272&from=LV] and [Chemical Substances Law|https://likumi.lv/ta/en/en/id/47839-chemical-substances-law]:

# It is prohibited to sell toxic and very toxic chemical substances and mixtures to natural persons who are under 18 years of age.
# Natural or legal persons who sell toxic or very toxic substances or mixtures must maintain records of the purchasers of the abovementioned chemical substances or mixtures. Upon maintenance of records of the purchasers, the name and amount of the sold toxic or very toxic chemical substances and mixtures, and also the following must be indicated:
## for natural persons - the given name, surname and personal identity number of the purchaser;
for legal persons - registration number and registered office, name of the undertaking (company) or firm name of the company.
# Records of purchasers must be stored for 10 years according to the requirements of Article 36 of Regulation 1907/2006 and Article 49 of CLP Regulation and must be presented to the supervisory and control institutions at their request.
# Processing of personal data must be carried out in compliance with the laws and regulations governing the protection of personal data.

The Law does not specify how specifically it should be stored; however, it should be stored in such a way that it can be present to authorities upon their request. These products should be duly labelled pursuant to CPL Regulation.

*Correct labelling of the goods*. Most of the nicotine pouches in Latvian market contain the following labelling:

* They all contain exclamation mark pictogram (CLP designation - GHS07);
health wording "_Šis izstrādājums satur nikotīnu, kas ir stipru pieradumu izraisoša viela"_ _("This product contains nicotine which is a highly addictive substance”_).
pictogram with strikethrough of “18”;
warning that product contains nicotine and is hazardous;
instruction on what action is required if the pouch has been swallowed;
that it should be kept away from kids; as well as list of ingredients;
how much nicotine is in one unit;
best before date;
content;
and information about manufacturer and distributor.

It is recommended that products sold by you also comply with the same requirements.  

*Soon to be applied requirements*. Other requirements (analogy to [Tobacco Law|https://likumi.lv/ta/en/en/id/282077-on-the-handling-of-tobacco-products-herbal-products-for-smoking-electronic-smoking-devices-and-their-liquids]), indicated in the opinion of the Health Inspectorate should be regarded as recommendation; however, in such a way that it is complied with as much as it is possible given that currently amendments to the Tobacco law are reviewed in the parliament which after approved will apply the same requirements to nicotine pouches as to tobacco products, electronic smoking devices and liquids and so on. Which means, that these products will be prohibited to be sold via distance contract (online) and it will need the same labelling as products currently regulated under the Tobacco Law. As indicated in my previous email, you should apply especially high caution not to sell these products to individuals under 18 years of age.



*Importing requirements*. Please note that this product contains nicotine. Thus, it is most likely will be subject to Cabinet Regulation No. 795, adopted 22 December 2015. _“Procedures for Registration of Chemical Substances and Mixtures and Their Database”_[_\[1]_|https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#m_-9089050017185566132__ftn1] ([Regulation No 795|https://likumi.lv/ta/en/en/id/279100-procedures-for-registration-of-chemical-substances-and-mixtures-and-their-database]). The aforementioned stipulates that a person who manufactures the chemical substance or mixture or imports it in the territory of Latvia from another EU Member State or any country outside the EU must electronically register and complete the report on activities involving chemical substances and mixtures on the website of the state limited liability company “[Latvian Environment, Geology and Meteorology Centre|https://www.meteo.lv/en/lapas/about-centre?&id=1473]” upon entering into a contract with the Centre regarding the use of Joint Environmental Information System. The report on the previous calendar year must be submitted by 1 March of the current year. This requirement is applied if substances and mixtures imported or manufactured in the territory of Latvia exceeds 100 kilograms per year. It must be noted that merchants, who import nicotine liquids used in e-cigarettes in the aforementioned quantities, do comply with this requirement. Though, this requirement must be complied with only after one year of the relevant chemical substance or mixtures being imported or manufactured in the territory of Latvia. The report form, laid down in Annex of the Regulation 795, basically inquires identification of the entity or individual carrying out the specified activity with chemical substance or mixture, classification of the substance or the mixture, and quantity of it.

